{
  "id": "Compound::DB00761 - Gene::6560",
  "verbalization": "Potassium Chloride appears to interact with Slc12a4 through a series of molecular and functional pathways that involve cation-coupled chloride transport. The evidence suggests that Potassium Chloride binds to Slc12a6 and Slc12a5, which are both involved in cation-coupled chloride cotransport. These transporters are further implicated in the activity of Slc12a4, indicating a potential functional link between the two entities. The binding of Potassium Chloride to Slc12a6 and Slc12a5 may modulate the activity of Slc12a4, which is involved in the transport of chloride ions across cellular membranes. This relationship is supported by the presence of multiple pathways that connect Potassium Chloride to Slc12a4 through different molecular mechanisms, suggesting a complex but coherent functional interaction. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Slc12a4 in chloride transport and its potential regulation by Potassium Chloride through its interaction with Slc12a6 and Slc12a5.",
